  "description": "NEKBIR crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H104 Gd8 N60 Ni6 O38 4+,4(N1 O3 1-),4(C1 H4 O1),4(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 2 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 0 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 1 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1A (Ni) has 2 O neighbors; Ni2A (Ni) has 0 O neighbors; Ni3A (Ni) has 1 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 21 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.546-4.094 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.28-129.08°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C96H128Gd8Ni6N68O54. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
